  "body": "**Status: independent verification.** The construction claims of record candidate #2269 reproduce, and no counterexample was found. Evidence, metadata and accounting defects are listed below. There is no new \u03ba, no frontier change, and no endorsement of \u03ba beyond what is checked here.\n\n## Object\n\n#2269 (jeremykothe2, head `b479fc5567bc09ab9185bffe89b62594f36d74e5`, `research/gmx-t74-borrow43/`) claims conditional \u03ba = 0.0016962471390584742\u2026, which is +1.4% over the selected record. It adds 43 borrowed-helper aliases from #2226 (Cinna Davis' anticipatory dirty borrowing) to the T74 pivot-566+554 words and re-fills the 666-call hosting.\n\nWhen this check started, nothing committed independently checked the new 437-helper fill. The shipped `evidence/INDEPENDENT.json` describes a different, pre-borrow 480-helper fill.\n\n## What reproduces, using fresh stdlib code\n\nThe new code imports, executes and copies no code from #2269, #2226 or #2260. The longest shared token run against 19 PR scripts is 27 tokens. All 40 inputs are pinned by git blob id and sha256.\n\n**Words.** For both `BORROW-WORD-43{base,extra}`:\n- **Warps:** all 43 have G invertible over GF(2), dim U = dim E, G\u00b7span U = span E, and K_G mapping L_U to L_E, so the Fourier rank is 0.\n- **No anticipatory terms:** every alias is a \"high\" alias.\n- **Frames:** frame climbs are nested.\n- **Exact replay** over \u211a\u27e8F\u2084\u2083\u27e9, with arbitrary dirty registers:\n  - Y\u1d62 \u2190 Y\u1d62 + X\u1d62;\n  - the other 549 live registers and the 76 zero buffers are restored;\n  - the dual orientation also replays.\n- **Recounted profiles:**\n  - 43base `{1:2351,2:501,3:414,4:129,5:42,8:8}`;\n  - 43extra `{1:2339,2:509,3:418,4:125,5:42,8:8}`;\n  - mass 5385, 437 helpers, widths `{4:36,5:9,7:36,8:116,9:240}`.\n\n**Fill.** For `OWNERS.json.gz`, 291,042 rows:\n- exactly one role per (call, live helper), and the removed helpers are absent;\n- widths match the words;\n- 1,332 windows are rebuilt from the event stream, they equal PLAN, and every role lies strictly inside its window;\n- families and namespaces are correct, with no role on the caller's active pair;\n- slices are disjoint, within their child, and prefix-filled across 149,184 bins;\n- the idle recount is `{1:23976,3:8673,5:813,7:150,48:24479}`.\n\n**Price.**\n- The global profile composed from *our* recounts equals `PROFILE.json`.\n- A fresh certified atanh/exp evaluator brackets the moment root to width 1e-130. The bracket contains the claimed b, and `complex_lower` + 1e-90 is rejected.\n- The \u03ba arithmetic from b is checked.\n\n**Positive controls.**\n- The canonical words reproduce the old {5:82} profiles.\n- The T37 parent fill reproduces its own spec.\n- Every script has targeted negative controls.\n\nThe gain attributable to borrowing is \u0394b = 1.64922\u00b710\u207b\u2075 over #2044's b.\n\n## Defects and open obligations (none changes b as checked)\n\n1. **No admission receipt for the borrowed supplier.**\n   - 8 evidence and metadata files are byte-identical to the pre-borrow #2044 package, including `evidence/INDEPENDENT.json`, `evidence/ASSEMBLY.json`, `evidence/FULL-ADMISSION.json`, `PRICE.json` and the top-level `SPEC.json`.\n   - The top-level PLAN and SPEC disagree with each other.\n2. **The 76 cleanup zero buffers per call are unpriced.**\n   - #2269's emitter allocates them eagerly, giving a peak of 513 fields against 480 unborrowed.\n   - `physical_stock_identity` has no buffer term. #2260 charged its buffers, and #2226 PROOF \u00a74 lists this as open.\n   - Charging them as dedicated families leaves the finite constants unchanged. Hosting them in idle children would move b; that case was not evaluated.\n3. **X2 is not checked.** That is pending-axis disjointness across children sharing a family, and it applies to 37,408 of 54,145 hosted families. The 73-column charts are not checked either. A failure would change the idle profile and therefore b.\n4. **Metadata errors:**\n   - `CLAIM.json` sets `construction_improvement: false`;\n   - the gain field mixes the outer and strict \u03ba;\n   - the README's lineage and width wording is wrong;\n   - stale numbers remain in the outer notes.\n\n## Not checked\n\n- the outer stack behind \u03ba = b (PR1673, PR1758, PR1786 and the union schedule); only b \u2192 \u03ba arithmetic is checked here, and #2286 inventoried that outer at #2044's point;\n- the native lowering and the exact Clifford lifts of K_G; the borrowing gain rests on the rank-zero handoffs, and charging warps as plain frame changes would give local mass 5581;\n- the 47 strict inequalities and the bootstrap;\n- inherited T74 and PR589 premises;\n- successor #2288's refit gauge44 word.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-borrow43-independent-check/check_all.py --fetch\n```\n\nThis takes about 35 s. `--fetch` fetches `refs/pull/2269/head` only if `b479fc55` is absent; every input is still verified against its pins. Expected last line:\n\n```text\nPASS_T74_BORROW43_INDEPENDENT_CHECK words=PASS fill=PASS price=PASS runner_controls=3 commit=b479fc5567bc mode=git\n```\n\nChecks run locally:\n- the runner passes from the repo root and from `/tmp`;\n- `research_package.py --check-only` passes;\n- the 65 `test_research_*` tests pass;\n- the Python 3.12 registered replay was **not** run (3.12 is not installed), and the scripts parse under the 3.10 grammar.\n\n## Provenance and credit\n\n- **Base:** `0fdd7d82` (priority revision 4), unchanged at submission (2026-10-15 04:53 UTC).\n- **Track and claim:** track 75\u201384, OS seed 76. No sprint coordination issue exists, so the claim was recorded locally. Card: `independent-moment`, refined.\n- **Credit:**\n  - Jeremy Kothe (#2269, T74 lineage);\n  - Cinna Davis / 1337isnot1337 (#2226);\n  - Dugongue (#2260);\n  - the T74 lineage (PR1319/1625/1297);\n  - icekylinx (checker lineage).\n- **Related:** #2311, from the same account in a separate session, independently audits the different #2260/#2265 T8 supplier; it is complementary.\n\nPrepared for Sagar Thakrar with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic). Separate agents wrote the three checks; two adversarial reviewers checked independence and coverage; the main session reran every command. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
